  "question": {
    "text": "A vessel with square cross-section and height of 6 m is vertically partitioned. A small window of $100 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$ with hinged door is fitted at a depth of 3 m in the partition wall. One part of the vessel is filled completely with water and the other side is filled with the liquid having density $1.5 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$. What force one needs to apply on the hinged door so that it does not get opened ?<br/>(Acceleration due to gravity $=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/QnnD4h1-8KDWXRRahwDwMf-_2g4pVyui-khBkGc-sBY.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>in equilibrium<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{F}_{\\text {ext }}+\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{w}}=\\mathrm{F}_{\\ell} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{F}_{\\text {ext }}=\\mathrm{F}_{\\ell}-\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{w}} \\\\ & =\\left(\\mathrm{P}_0+\\rho_{\\ell} \\mathrm{gh}\\right) \\mathrm{A}-\\left(\\mathrm{P}_0+\\rho_{\\mathrm{w}} \\mathrm{gh}\\right) \\mathrm{A} \\\\ & =\\left(\\rho_{\\ell}-\\rho_{\\mathrm{w}}\\right) \\mathrm{ghA} \\\\ & =(1500-1000) \\times 10 \\times 3 \\times\\left(100 \\times 10^{-4}\\right) \\\\ & =150 \\mathrm{~m}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
